\f0\b\fs48 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 VHSart \'97 IMPLEMENT UPPER STATIC BAND & CYAN-GREEN WASH\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Objective\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Reconstruct the supplied reference image 
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 IMG_4655.jpeg
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2  as a dedicated, fully procedural effect inside the native C++ After Effects plugin, VHSart.\
The reference has three distinctive visual components:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Upper Dense Horizontal Static Band:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  A very wide, dark, high-density horizontal interference region covering approximately 40\'9645% of the frame height, containing fragmented horizontal lines, colored static, scanline displacement, and intermittent bright/dark streaks.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	2.	}Lower-Right Cyan-Green Chroma Wash:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  A localized, soft, irregular cyan-green chromatic wash in the lower-right and middle-right portions of the image, interacting with a dark, irregular patch.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	3.	}Dark Analog Base:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  A predominantly dark, low-resolution image with restrained softness, subtle grain, and scattered horizontal interference lines outside the main upper band.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The visual identity depends on the contrast between the dense dark upper interference band and the localized pale cyan-green chromatic region below it.\
Reconstruct these characteristics procedurally. Do not use pre-rendered overlays, stock textures, images, video clips, GIFs, or baked-in reference material.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 1. Mandatory Project Inspection\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Before implementation:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Inspect the complete VHSart project structure and existing rendering architecture.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Identify existing engines for static noise, colored noise, tracking interference, horizontal tearing, scanlines, chroma displacement, chroma smearing, dropouts, grain, softness, and luminance processing.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Reuse or extend compatible existing engines.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Do not duplicate existing functionality.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Implement dedicated processing only for the distinctive upper static-band behavior and localized lower-right chroma wash.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Preserve all existing effects, presets, controls, and rendering behavior.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Inspect actual source implementations instead of assuming that existing engine names accurately describe their capabilities.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 2. Dedicated Engine Architecture\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement a dedicated hybrid engine:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Upper Static & Localized Chroma Wash Engine
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
It must contain three independently controllable processing systems:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 A. Upper Dense Static System\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Generates the wide upper horizontal static and chroma-luma interference band.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 B. Lower-Right Chroma Wash System\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Generates the localized cyan-green chromatic wash and its associated dark irregular region.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 C. Dark Analog Base System\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Reuses existing VHSart softness, luminance, grain, and scanline processing.\
These systems must have independent masks and controls.\
Do not combine them into one generic noise or color-overlay operation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 3. Upper Dense Horizontal Static Band\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Create a full-width upper interference region.\
Default vertical coverage:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Start: 0% of frame height.\
{\listtext	\'95	}End: approximately 40\'9645% of frame height.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal coverage: full frame width.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The band must be predominantly dark, with dense and irregular horizontal interference.\
Its internal appearance should include:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Dark gray and black horizontal structures.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Fragmented scanlines.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Colored noise particles and streaks.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Blue, green, red, cyan, violet, and magenta interference.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Occasional white and pale flashes.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Short horizontal displacement segments.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Uneven brightness interruptions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Irregular line lengths and gaps.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Localized RGB channel separation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Chroma and luminance interference.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The band must not look like a uniform rectangular block filled with random noise.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Internal Structure\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Generate multiple procedural layers:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Low-frequency dark horizontal structures.\
{\listtext	2.	}Medium-frequency fragmented interference lines.\
{\listtext	3.	}Fine high-frequency static.\
{\listtext	4.	}Sparse colored chromatic streaks.\
{\listtext	5.	}Occasional bright and dark dropout segments.\
{\listtext	6.	}Horizontal image displacement.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Each layer must have independently controllable contribution.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Horizontal Displacement\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Apply localized row-based horizontal displacement:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 sourceX = x - displacement(x, y, time, seed)
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Use irregular, segmented displacement rather than identical offsets across every scanline.\
The main geometric distortion must remain horizontal.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 4. Lower-Right Cyan-Green Chroma Wash\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Create a localized chromatic wash primarily in the lower-right and middle-right regions.\
The dominant colors should be:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Pale cyan.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Muted green.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Light green-cyan.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Pale gray-white.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Dark gray.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Black and muted brown-gray in the associated dark region.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The wash should resemble analog chromatic bleeding and localized color contamination, not a clean digital gradient.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Spatial Shape\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Use an adjustable irregular spatial mask with:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Configurable center position.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal radius.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Vertical radius.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Soft edges.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Organic boundary variation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Adjustable asymmetry.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Optional directional smearing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The default position should be toward the lower-right region, but the user must be able to reposition and resize it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Chromatic Processing\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Localized chroma displacement.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Cyan-green hue bias.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Soft chroma bleeding.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal chroma extensions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Controlled luminance interaction.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Irregular color transitions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Adjustable saturation and brightness.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The wash must interact with the underlying image and preserve visible image structure where appropriate.\
Do not simply paint a flat cyan-green shape over the footage.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 5. Dark Irregular Patch\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Reconstruct the dark, irregular region overlapping or adjoining the chroma wash.\
Generate it through a separate procedural luminance mask.\
Controls should include:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Enable Dark Patch.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Position.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal Size.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Vertical Size.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Edge Softness.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Darkness.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Irregularity.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Chroma Interaction.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The patch must have soft, irregular boundaries rather than a clean geometric rectangle or ellipse.\
Keep this system separate from the cyan-green chroma wash so both can be adjusted independently.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 6. Lower Horizontal Lines and Dropouts\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Outside the main upper band, add subtle horizontal interference lines across the lower portion of the image.\
These should include:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Sparse thin horizontal lines.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Short bright and dark segments.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Occasional colored streaks.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Minor horizontal displacement.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Low-to-medium noise density.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Keep these elements substantially less dense than the main upper static band.\
They must not accidentally recreate a second large tracking band.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 7. Dark Analog Base\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Reuse VHSart\'92s existing compatible engines to create:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Low-resolution analog character.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Subtle global softness.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Dark luminance balance.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Restrained global grain.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Fine scanlines.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Mild detail reduction.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The overall image should remain predominantly dark.\
Do not crush all shadows into pure black or destroy the lower-left image content.\
The lower-right cyan-green wash should remain visibly brighter than the surrounding dark image.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 8. Processing Pipeline\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Use the following logical order:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Existing low-resolution and softness processing.\
{\listtext	2.	}Existing base luminance and contrast processing.\
{\listtext	3.	}Existing global grain and fine scanlines.\
{\listtext	4.	}Upper static-band mask generation.\
{\listtext	5.	}Upper horizontal static and interference generation.\
{\listtext	6.	}Upper localized horizontal displacement.\
{\listtext	7.	}Lower-right chroma-wash mask generation.\
{\listtext	8.	}Cyan-green chroma bleeding and localized color processing.\
{\listtext	9.	}Dark irregular patch processing.\
{\listtext	10.	}Lower scattered horizontal lines and dropouts.\
{\listtext	11.	}Final compositing and alpha handling.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Adjust the exact order where required by the existing VHSart architecture, but preserve the independent behavior of each processing system.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

